From fecfcabb448c7100b9cba6f7a5bd80b78b50e01a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:55:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: Keep the pipelines Metal builds in archives of each
 game's

Metal keeps the pipelines it builds in a cache of each app's, Wine's
for every game, which stays at about 2.4 GB. Rise of the Tomb Raider
creates its 13,659 pipelines at every start; after another game or
driver build Metal built them all again, about 2,000 s on the compile
threads, during the game's own benchmark.

Keep them in Metal 4 archives in kosmickrisp_pipelines/<process> next
to Mesa's shader cache instead: pipelines come from the archives when
they are there, and the ones Metal builds are captured and written to
a new archive every 1,024 pipelines, 5 s after the last one and when
the last device goes. Writing must not overlap pipeline builds, Metal
crashes, so they wait for it. Metal can't add to an archive: with more
than 32 of them, the next process captures every pipeline it creates
into a new generation, and the one after drops the older generations.
MESA_KK_PIPELINE_ARCHIVES=0 turns them off.

Rise of the Tomb Raider after a run with another driver: pipelines
take 37 instead of 1,900 s on the compile threads, the benchmark 125
instead of 227 s, the mean is 22.3 instead of 19.0 fps.

Generated-by: LLM
